<title>JAPAN: US auto makers want 100 to 110 yen to dollar -- Card.</title>
<headline>US auto makers want 100 to 110 yen to dollar -- Card.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. auto industry wants to see a dollar at between 100 yen to 110 yen, Andrew Card, president of the American Automobile Manufacturers Association, told Reuters Financial Television on Monday.</p>
<p>Speaking on a visit to Tokyo, Card said that he did not believe in government interference in exchange rates.</p>
<p>But he said, &quot;I personally would like to see the dollar at about 100 yen, but when it's over 110, I think we're in trouble. So, it should be in the 100 to 110 yen range.&quot;</p>
</text>
